[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Slav Defence"]
[Variation "Slav Defence, Quiet Variation"]
[ECO "D11"]
[Character "solid,tactical"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,discovered-attack"]
[Themes "light-bishop-out,h-file-attack"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. e3 Bf5 { Brings the light bishop out before ...e6 can lock it in. } 5. Nf3 ( 5. cxd5 cxd5 { Keeps a pawn on d5 and opens the c-file. } 6. Qb3 Nc6 { Develops a piece and attacks the pawn on d4. } ) 5... e6 6. Nh4 { Attacks the bishop on f5. } 6... Bg6 { Keeps the bishop; if White takes it, Black gets the h-file for the rook. } 7. Nxg6 hxg6 { Retakes with the h-pawn, not the f-pawn, so the rook gets the open h-file and points at h2. } 8. Bd3 Bd6 { Aims at h2 and the g3 square. [%cal Gd6h2] }
9. O-O? ( 9. g3 O-O 10. O-O ) 9... Bxh2+ { Wins a pawn with check. The king cannot take the bishop, because the rook on h8 guards h2 along the open h-file. } 10. Kh1 Bc7+ { Moving the bishop gives a discovered check from the rook on h8, because the h-file is now open to the king. } *
